<title>INDIA: India M3 money supply falls to 15.8 pct on Mar 14.</title>
<headline>India M3 money supply falls to 15.8 pct on Mar 14.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth was 15.8 percent on March 14, 1997, down from 15.9 percent on February 28, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Saturday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   Mar 14, 1997   Feb 28, 1997  Mar 15, 1996</p>
<p>			15.8	    15.9		14.8</p>
<p>Money supply was 6,830.24 billion rupees on March 14, 1997 against 6,783.77 billion rupees on February 28, 1997 and compared to 5,875.68 on March 15, 1996 the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
